The rewrite caches the vector's base pointer and size once, then scans with a plain pointer. This removes the repeated `size()` reload and the `int` cast in the loop condition. It still calls `GetNum()` and returns the first match, so behavior is unchanged. Expect only a small speedup, since the original loop was already simple.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field* p = fields.data();
    Field* const end = p + fields.size();
    for (; p != end; ++p)
    {
        if (p->GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return p;
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```